    wrong for most readers and large.

.claude/skills/{brand-review,campaign-plan,competitive-brief,content-creation,
                draft-content,email-sequence,performance-report,seo-audit}
    Marketing skills, from Anthropic's knowledge-work-plugins marketplace.
    Apache Licence, Version 2.0. Full text at .claude/marketing/LICENSE,
    alongside the upstream README and CONNECTORS reference they cite.

    Vendored unmodified but for one path: each SKILL.md links to CONNECTORS.md
    relative to its plugin root, and that file now sits at
    .claude/marketing/CONNECTORS.md, so the link was repointed there. Nothing
    else was changed.

The two skill sets above are redistributed under Apache 2.0 §4, which is why
their licence text travels with them and the modifications are recorded rather
than summarised. Neither is required for the repository to build, test or run:
delete either directory and nothing else breaks.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Adapted components under packages/ui/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

packages/ui/src/assistant/
    Beautiful UI — https://www.beautifului.dev
    Copyright (c) 2026 Shane Levine
    MIT Licence. The full text is reproduced below.

    `answer.tsx`, `tool-chip.tsx`, `approval-card.tsx` and the stylesheet
    `beautiful-ui.css` are adapted from that library's Streaming Text, Tool
    Chips, Approval Card and foundation stylesheet. They were changed rather
    than copied: the components are driven by this application's data instead
    of the originals' scripted demos, the Approval Card was reduced from a
    multi-question wizard to the single proposal this product actually makes,
    and the stylesheet defines Beautiful UI's token names in terms of
    `@vantion/tokens` rather than shipping a second palette. `prompt-bar.tsx`
    and `conversation.tsx` are this repository's own work in the same visual
    language.

